---
// src/pages/how-to-extract-attachments-from-mbox.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const SEO_TITLE = "How to Extract Attachments from MBOX Files Online Free";
const SEO_DESC = "Learn how to extract PDF, image, and document attachments from large MBOX and Google Takeout files directly in your browser without software.";
---

<Layout title={SEO_TITLE} description={SEO_DESC}>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 prose prose-slate">
    <div class="mb-8">
      <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-sky-600 uppercase tracking-wider">Tutorial & Guide</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-2 mb-4">
        How to Extract Attachments from MBOX Files
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm">Save photos, contracts, and PDF documents from your email archives</p>
    </div>

    <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
      When people download their Gmail or Thunderbird archives, their primary objective is often finding lost attachments: old tax receipts, business contracts, legal PDFs, or family photos sent years ago.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-4">How Attachments Are Stored in MBOX</h2>
    <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
      MBOX files do not store attachments in a separate folder. Instead, files are encoded directly into the text stream using <strong>Base64 MIME encoding</strong> (RFC 2045). This makes manual extraction in text editors like Notepad or TextEdit impossible, as the file appears as thousands of lines of random characters.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-8 mb-4">Step-by-Step Attachment Extraction with ViewMbox</h2>
    <ol class="text-sm text-slate-600 space-y-3 mb-8">
      <li><strong>Load Archive:</strong> Open <a href="/" class="text-sky-600 underline">ViewMbox.com</a> and drop your MBOX file.</li>
      <li><strong>Locate Message:</strong> Use the search bar to filter by sender or subject line.</li>
      <li><strong>View Attachment Pills:</strong> When you click a message containing files, ViewMbox automatically detects and decodes the MIME parts, displaying attachment badges at the top of the email view.</li>
      <li><strong>1-Click Download:</strong> Click any attachment badge to save the original PDF, image, or document directly to your Downloads folder.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="text-center pt-6 not-prose">
      <a href="/" class="inline-block bg-sky-600 hover:bg-sky-700 text-white font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded-full shadow-sm text-sm transition">
        Extract MBOX Attachments Now →
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
